      "content": "[https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=IIyBfvgz0FA](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=IIyBfvgz0FA)  \n**Live Science | Nik Murzin | Qubit Onion**  \nWolfram Institute \n\n<columns>\n\n\nI believe that the Cube is the three 3D +/- axes. That is the Qubit space. \n\nThere are two interpenetrating tetrahedra within the Cube, and also he is tracing out this outer/larger Tet. \n\nThe cube could be chosen to have unit basis 1, or the inner or outer Tet edge could have length 1. \n\n\n\n\n\n|||\n\n[https://coda.io/d/_d0SvdI3KSto/_suQWY5DS](https://coda.io/d/_d0SvdI3KSto/_suQWY5DS) \n\n  \nThe Synergetics Hierarchy of Concentric Polyhedra  \n[https://www.grunch.net/synergetics/volumes2.html](https://www.grunch.net/synergetics/volumes2.html)\n\n\n\nkirby urner may be interesting, seeing the [https://coda.io/d/_d0SvdI3KSto/_suF26nFn](https://coda.io/d/_d0SvdI3KSto/_suF26nFn) namespace reckoning with the cosmic shape hierarchy. \n\n[https://groups.io/g/synergeo/message/2735](https://groups.io/g/synergeo/message/2735)\n\n \n\n(All denominated in whole-integer volumes in [https://coda.io/d/_d0SvdI3KSto/_suSt6qdu](https://coda.io/d/_d0SvdI3KSto/_suSt6qdu) Quadray  \n{\"Title\":\"Quadray coordinates\",\"Summary\":{\"type\":\"slate\",\"root\":{\"children\":[{\"children\":[{\"text\":\"Coordinate system\"}],\"id\":\"cl-0\",\"style\":\"Paragraph\",\"type\":\"Line\",\"alignment\":\"Left\",\"lineLevel\":0}]}},\"Body\":{\"type\":\"slate\",\"root\":{\"children\":[{\"children\":[{\"text\":\"Quadray coordinates\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\", also known as \"},{\"text\":\"caltrop\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\", \"},{\"text\":\"tetray\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\" or \"},{\"text\":\"Chakovian\",\"bold\":true},{\"text\":\" coordinates (named for David Chako), were developed by Darrel Jarmusch (in 1981) and others, as another take on simplicial coordinates, a coordinate system using a simplex or tetrahedron as its basis polyhedron. \"}],\"id\":\"cl-0\",\"style\":\"Paragraph\",\"type\":\"Line\",\"alignment\":\"Left\",\"lineLevel\":0},{\"children\":[{\"text\":\" \"}],\"id\":\"cl-1\",\"style\":\"Paragraph\",\"type\":\"Line\",\"alignment\":\"Left\",\"lineLevel\":0}]}},\"Url\":{\"type\":\"urlref\",\"url\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Quadray_coordinates\",\"name\":\"\"},\"LastEdited\":{\"type\":\"dt\",\"input\":\"7/5/2024 12:01:17 AM\",\"epoch\":1720162877}}\n\n\n\n|||\n\nGroup, permutations. \n\n[https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Galois_theory](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Galois_theory)\n\n[https://mathworld.wolfram.com/GaloisGroup.html](https://mathworld.wolfram.com/GaloisGroup.html)\n\n[https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Galois_group](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Galois_group)\n\nGalois, Abel.\n\nNoticing that looking at Field Extensions (factorized Polynomials), taking the Rational numbers and adding sqrt(2). Field (of e.g. Rationals), then adding the Extension of sqrt(2), sqrt(3), i, etc. with structural similarity. And groups that structure that.\n\nCan prove that with certain Polynomial, with needing a certain kind of group for permuting them — if it is not solvable (able to be broken down normally with quotients to the trivial/basal group case).  \n\nCannot solve for the Quintic case. \n\n\n\nPart 2 from 10-10-2024  \n[https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=rHuBrpkb_4U](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=rHuBrpkb_4U)  \n**Live Science | Qubits in Phase Space and the Quantum Potato Chip**\n\n\n\n\n\nNested Tet’s\n\n\n\n.\n\n.\n\n\n</columns>\n\nRandom meme: ",
